        {
          "text": "From 6 April 2027, most unused defined contribution pensions and death benefits (such as drawdown funds and uncrystallised pots) will be included in your taxable estate for IHT. Exceptions include pensions paid to a surviving spouse or civil partner, dependents\u0027 scheme pensions, and death-in-service benefits. Executors will be responsible for declaring pension values as part of the IHT return and may use new options for settling any tax due directly from pension funds.",
